**Romis** ( /'*roːmis* /, [[rastreshani|Rastreshani]]: *ᕈᒥᔅ*, romanized: rumis, [[eumosa|Eumosa]]: *𐐡𐐬𐑋𐐨𐑅*) is one of the seven elemental deities. She is bound to the element of Astral and she is the god of stars, magic and dreams. She is the deity who is responsible for the balance of the planes.

# Religion
The *Micoan*[^micoan] religion is a more science based religion, mostly formed by artificers and wizards. It integrates the historical base of religion and knowledge with the modern scientific thinking. With the help of Romis, the *Micoatl*[^micoatl] have build many temples, which also act as observatories. The main belief of the *Micoan* religion is: "Belief in your own knowledge.". 

On many planar based subjects, they investigate on their own and draw their own conclusion, but for the astral subjects and predictions of the future they look towards Romis. They have a individual form of communion, akin to meditation, called *Equistal*[^equistal]. In this communion they have vision of exploring the stars and the universe. Through this means and reading the leylines, they are able to divine predictions on many different subjects. The temples of Romis also serve as Observatories. These are used to make different starmaps for different region. Using these, they are able to assign starsigns to people, usually they differ per 5 years cycles. 

The observatories, formally called *Pavansern*[^pavansern], are large round stone building built in clearing or on hill-/mountaintops. On top there is a large dome, split open by the large telescope poking through.^[These are always on a north-south axis] Above the entrance there is a unique leadlight artwork, somehow featuring the *Aurora Star*.

Their followers are named the *Micoatl*, they adopted this name from other religions. They would mock them for their love of the Quetzalcoatl, yet they later adopted the name in pride. A large portion of the *Micoatl* are [[coatl|Coatl]]'s. Quetzalcoatl hold a special place in the *Micoan* religion as they are believed to have come directly form the Astral Sea. Many reside near to observatories for their protections, as wings of a Coatl sell for lots of gold.

In the early [[decemvir-era|Decemvir Era]], there was a convention of mages, wizards and artificers. This *Convention of the Divine*  was a election of their new patron deity. After their previous deity *Shaagi* passed away. Romis was eventually chosen and would ascend to the Astral element domain with her new gained power. The other candidates were: Sydtarr, Ezotl, Davarin, Ohygyn and Igtar, of which this is the only surviving record.

## Sects
The *Credo*'s are sects in the *Micoan*[^micoan] religion, which operate in different subjects. They frequently exchange tomes of knowledge. 

* Credo of **Etoiles**
The Credo of Etoiles are those which are actively researching the Astral Plane and it's many star from this plane. They are able to read the stars using the *Stella Lingua*'s[^sl] described alphabet.
* Credo of **Tans**
Tans is the Credo who are predicting the future by prophesying. They use *Equistal*[^equistal] and the *Stella Lingua*[^sl] to attempt to predict the future of the world. Their commonly called the timekeepers as their hold over the future is monopolistic.
* Credo of **Charaut**
Charaut is the Credo ever pushing the bound of magic. They want to control the magics they have been gifted. Many hours have been poured into discovering the origin of them. Many mages and wizards contribute to this ever-growing experiment.
* Credo of **Sain**
The Credo of Sain, nicknamed the *Hospitaller*[^hospitaller], will care and heal everyone. They view the preservation of every life as essential. They actively collaborate with the <a href="aenar">Aenarian</a> religion in their Hospitals. 
* Credo of **Agir'sur**
The Credo of Agir'sur are the credo of the artificers. They are constantly pushing the boundaries of construction. They have managed to construct evermore impressive works, even giving life to their constructions.

## Structure
### Venerated Ancestors
*See also: [[list-of-micoan-venerated-ancestors|List of Micoan Venerated Ancestors]]*
In History there are those people which single-handedly push boundaries. In the *Micoan*[^micoan] religion these are revered as saints. Them and their works are studied and bewildered by all. They are given the prefix of *Thakur*[^thakur], the works are then known as a *Thakurain*[^thakurain].

### Priestly Order
There is no central authority in the *Micoan*[^micoan] religion. They instead rely on communal desc ions made in one of many *Conventions*. Subjects and motions are submitted by the attendees and debates, which led by the *Debatemaster*. Finally they will vote on each of them, as such making the decisions. 

# Cultural
## Stella Lingua[^sl]
The *Stella Lingua* is the central artifact and script of the *Micoan*[^micoan] religion. It is heavily copied an d being researched. The words must be thousands of years old, as the words have led to such monumental breakthroughs. It described the reasoning and methods of prophesying from a *Starmap* or a *Equistal*[^equistal]. 

## Oracle of Discovery
The Oracle of Discovery is a institution of the *Micoan*[^micoan] religion based all around the world. It accepts requests for prophecy and return the results later. These requests are delivered to the many Hall of Oracles around the world, where oracles divine their answers. This where the incredible amount of money they own is made.

## Starlight Faire
The *Starlight Faire* is the holy day of Romis, celebrated by most of the religions all around the world. This is because the celebrations are sponsored by the *Micoan* [^micoan]religion and the Oracle of Discovery. It is a night time celebration of the Past, Present and Future, featuring wines and beers, music and dancing, starlight and late nights. 

